# Copyrighted MAME ROM dumps used only for local sim/sor_board_tb.sv
# runs — never commit these, extract from offroad.zip locally instead.
#
# roms_src/ holds per-game extracted dumps (offroadt/, pigout/) and was NOT
# covered by the sim/*.uNN patterns below -- every file in it was untracked
# and addable, i.e. one `git add -A` away from being published. Added
# 2026-07-26.
roms_src/
sim/*.u58t
sim/*.u59t
sim/*.u57t
sim/*.u56t
sim/*.u3
sim/*.u67
sim/*.u69
sim/*.u90
sim/*.u92
sim/*.u93
sim/*.u94
sim/*.u95
sim/*.u4t
sim/*.u5t
sim/*.u6t
sim/*.u7t
sim/*.u8t
sim/*.u13t
sim/*.u14t
sim/*.u15t
sim/*.u25t
sim/*.u26t
sim/*.u27t

# ModelSim build/run artifacts -- regenerated locally by sim/README.md's
# vlog/vsim commands, never useful to commit.
sim/work/
sim/transcript
sim/vsim.wlf
sim/log.lot
sim/modelsim.ini
sim/sim_output.log
sim/sim_run*.log
sim/master_pc_trace.log
sim/slave_pc_trace.log
sim/__pycache__/
quartus_build*.log

# WP10 sound bring-up: per-run scratch (waveform captures, PC/register
# dumps, Lua/Tcl one-off scripts, ModelSim work dirs) generated repeatedly
# during hardware-diagnostic iteration -- never useful to commit, unlike
# the actual RTL/testbench sources they were generated by.
sim/work_*/
sim/sva_work/
sim/*.log
sim/*.pcm
sim/*.wav
sim/*.png
sim/*.ppm
sim/*.vstf
sim/*.lua
sim/*.tcl
sim/*_result.txt
sim/*_results.txt
sim/*_dump.txt
sim/*_dump.bin
sim/*.bin
sim/*.txt
# ...but the file lists ARE sources, not scratch. sim/*.txt above had silently
# swallowed sim/flist_board_verilator.txt, so the Verilator flow (the primary
# validation gate) was absent from a fresh clone entirely -- along with
# sim/mt48lc16m16a2_vl.v, which the flist references and which is simply never
# added. Both are now tracked; keep new flists tracked too.
!sim/flist_*.txt
quartus_fgck_build.log
report_timing_wp10*
build_deploy_pipeline.log
/transcript
/sim_promst_check2.log

# Per-run scratch that had accumulated untracked at the repo root and under
# sim/, making `git status` unreadable (~90 entries) and easy to lose real
# changes in. All regenerated by the documented build/sim commands.
/build_*.log
/sta_*.txt
/sta_probe*.log
/work_*/
sim/verilator/
sim/vout_*/

# Reference source dumps (MAME driver/core source, other MiSTer cores'
# RTL) pulled in locally for research -- kept off-repo now that this
# project is going public; not our code, not worth carrying as history.
docs/reference/mame/
docs/reference/Arcade-Tempest_MiSTer/

